    "title": {
     "en": "Rain, rain, come again"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "What comes down but never goes up? Rain! Watch the sky every day for a week and guess whether it will rain."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "rain",
     "raindrops",
     "clues",
     "water"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Welcome to Water, A Precious Gift. Let us begin with the rain.\nWatch the sky every day for a week. Will it rain today? Your guess may be right on some days and wrong on others.\nLook for clues such as dark clouds, wind, a damp smell or hot weather. Ask an elder how they guess.\nWhen it rains, ask questions. Is it heavy or light? Are the drops big or small? Do they fall fast or slow? Is it slanting or straight?\nRain is a main source of water. We also get water from rivers, ponds, wells and taps (additional, not in the textbook).\nWater is used for drinking, cooking, bathing and washing."
    }
